---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
import ContactInvitation from './ContactInvitation.astro';
import EditorialModel from './EditorialModel.astro';
import {getIndustries} from '../data/content';
interface Props {draft?:boolean;}
const {draft=false}=Astro.props;
const fields=await getIndustries(draft);
---
<Layout noindex={draft} title='Company' description='NRTH Inc. is an independent company bringing distinct venture directions together across six fields. Meet the thinking behind NRTH.'>
 {draft&&<aside class='preview-banner'><a href='/preview'>Editorial workspace</a><span data-preview-status>Draft preview</span></aside>}
 <section class='page-heading'><span class='section-label'>The company</span><h1>Not one lane.<br/><em>A wider world.</em></h1><p>NRTH brings nine venture directions into one wider view of the work around us. Different disciplines. Specific questions. Room to see what connects them.</p><a class='inline-link' href='#company-model'>Explore how NRTH fits together</a></section>
 <div id='company-model'><EditorialModel kind='company' dark/></div>
 <dl class='facts-list'><div><dt>Company</dt><dd>NRTH Inc.</dd></div><div><dt>Portfolio</dt><dd>Nine ventures</dd></div><div><dt>Perspective</dt><dd>Six fields</dd></div><div><dt>Find us</dt><dd>nrth.group</dd></div></dl>
 <section class='editorial-split'><div data-enter><span class='section-label'>A way of thinking</span><h2>Stay curious.<br/>Get specific.</h2></div><div data-enter><p>A broad perspective is useful when it leads to a better question. We begin with the person doing the work, the information they need and the practical constraints around their decision.</p><p>A delayed shipment, an unclear health handoff and a fragmented software workflow have different stakes. Each deserves its own expertise. The connection is an interest in understanding the friction before proposing an answer.</p><div class='editorial-callout'><h3>The context comes first.</h3><p>Our public portfolio introduces the subjects we are exploring. A conversation about a specific venture establishes its current scope, the relevant requirements and what a practical next step could involve.</p></div><a class='inline-link' href='/approach'>How we approach an idea</a></div></section>
 <section class='editorial-split section-dark'><div data-enter><span class='section-label'>Room for difference</span><h2>The point is<br/>the perspective.</h2></div><div class='disclosure-list' data-enter><details open><summary>Keep the venture focused.<Icon name='plus'/></summary><div><p>A health workflow and a transport assignment need different knowledge, evidence and boundaries. Start with the purpose of that venture, the people it affects and the decisions it is meant to inform.</p><p>Relevant expertise should shape the direction. A general software pattern cannot establish clinical suitability, just as a vehicle signal cannot explain an operational exception without context.</p></div></details><details><summary>Let knowledge travel.<Icon name='plus'/></summary><div><p>A way to clarify responsibility, communicate uncertainty or test an interface can inform more than one field. The useful connection is a method or a question, rather than an assumption that every project should behave the same way.</p><p>For example, the idea of a visible handoff can prompt questions about care coordination, shipment ownership or an event production schedule. Each field determines what that handoff actually needs.</p></div></details><details><summary>Make room to change.<Icon name='plus'/></summary><div><p>Research can sharpen an idea, expose a constraint or suggest a different direction. Record what was examined, what was learned and which assumptions remain open.</p><p>Continuing is one possible result. Revising the question, seeking another perspective or setting an idea aside can be equally useful when the evidence points there.</p></div></details></div></section>
 <section class='editorial-split'><div data-enter><span class='section-label'>The worlds we work in</span><h2>Wide interests.<br/>Specific questions.</h2><p class='editorial-route-reference'>Each field guide explores the context, questions and venture directions behind that part of the portfolio.</p></div><div class='related-links editorial-field-links' data-enter>{fields.map(field=><a href={'/industries/'+field.name.toLowerCase()}><strong>{field.name}</strong><span>{field.copy}<br/>{field.ventures.map(name=>'NRTH '+name).join(' · ')}</span></a>)}</div></section>
 <ContactInvitation headline='See something differently?'/>
</Layout>
